                        "glosses": [
                            "An apparatus for determining the temperature of a distant point, by a thermoelectric circuit or otherwise."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b78aace-79df-4e7f-b40b-ecd186b570c4",
                                "sense_id": "75157c2b-a117-3ec2-8bb2-62265d9d738d",
                                "text": "\"The accurate measurement of temperature is still a problem of considerable difficulty,\" he resumed, adjusting the thermometer. \"A heated mass can impart vibratory motion to the ether which fills space, and the wave-motions of ether are able to reproduce in other bodies motions similar to those by which they are caused. At this end of the line I merely measure the electromotive force developed by the difference in temperature of two similar thermo-electric junctions, opposed. We call those junctions in a thermopile 'couples,' and by getting the recording instruments sensitive enough, we can measure one one-thousandth of a degree."
                            }
